  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "A feature that would be real nice is an \"upload code\". Where it lets people upload for someone who doesnt want to download ~5GB worth of stuff just to upload a character :/\n\nThis would be useful especially for commissioners that have clients who dont know the upload process, don't have the tools downloaded for it or simply dont wanna go through the motions of setting up a full on unity project with all the packages used\n\nRight now if i were to upload for someone that doesnt know or doesnt want to do all this, id have to have their log in info, which can be a major security concern.\n\nIn my opinion, the safest way to do this is generating a random code on the fly on the reciever's end, which is valid for one use only and turns invalid once the creator uploads a character with that code inserted somewhere in the SDK. The avatar then appears on the client's end next time they log in with a pop up that lets them accept or deny the upload. \n\nThis would improve QOL so much for creators that work with commissioned avatars.",
